# Line endings: LF on every host. A text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF whatever core.autocrlf or core.eol the host sets.
# Git for Windows and the hosted Windows runners default to autocrlf=true, which writes CRLF and breaks every byte-for-byte or hashed
# comparison of a checked-in file: docs/RELEASE-EXPORTS.md in release-exports.test.mjs, the Swift Right Suite API projection in
# scripts/gen-suite-api.mjs (rightkit#1175, #1187). One default removes that class instead of pinning each such file after it fails; `auto` leaves
# binary files alone. Later lines override this one per path. scripts/preflight.mjs eol-policy (G04) refuses a CRLF blob under it.
* text=auto eol=lf
# cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only batch files (labels and goto), so these keep CRLF on every host. None is tracked today.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Known binary formats by extension; auto-detection above is only a heuristic.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pb binary
*.bin binary
